<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine wheat growers urge gov't to join forces.</title>
<headline>Argentine wheat growers urge gov't to join forces.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentine wheat growers on Wednesday urged the government to join forces to gain new markets by boosting output and enhancing quality.</p>
<p>The Argentine Association of Wheat Producers said that during a meeting with Agriculture Secretary Felipe Sola they called for a firm policy of investments to boost store capacity.</p>
<p>In a press release they also expressed the need to work together to improve the grain markets transparency and to update futures markets.</p>
<p>The wheat producers deemed necessary to simplify norms regulating harvest equipment and called the government to fully enforce norms deregulating freight.</p>
<p>(-Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650)</p>
</text>
